!! 1. Keyboard shortcuts

You can create cards without touching the mouse. TiddlyFlashcards ships with these shortcuts:

| !Action | !Shortcut |
|Switch to the next (right) tab |<kbd>alt+L</kbd> |
|Switch to the previous (left) tab |<kbd>alt+H</kbd> |
|Focus the next (lower) field |<kbd>alt+J</kbd> |
|Focus the previous (upper) field |<kbd>alt+K</kbd> |
|Save the card |<kbd>alt+N</kbd> |
|Discard the draft |<kbd>alt+Delete</kbd> |

The editor tabs follow the note type order in the table below. You can rebind every shortcut in <kbd>~$:/Control Panel</kbd> ➡  <kbd>Keyboard Shortcuts</kbd>.

!! 2. Creating Cards

Each note type maps to a built-in Anki note type, so there is little to learn:

| !TiddlyFlashcards note type | !Anki note type | !Fields | !Notes |
|TFBasic |Basic |Front, Back |A plain question and answer. |
|TFCloze |Cloze |Text (required), Back Extra |The answer is hidden inside the text with cloze markers, so one note can produce several cards. See below. |
|TFType |type in the answer |Front, Back |In Anki you type the answer and it is checked against `Back`. |
|TFPair |Basic (and reversed card) |Front, Back |Produces two cards: Front → Back and Back → Front. |
|TFOptionalPair |Basic (optional reversed card) |Front, Back, Add Reverse |Produces the reverse card only when `Add Reverse` is non-empty, for example `yes`. |

Pick a tab, fill in the fields, then press <kbd>alt+N</kbd>. Every field is required except `Back Extra` on `TFCloze` and `Add Reverse` on `TFOptionalPair`.

!! 3. Making Cloze Cards

For a cloze note, `Text` is required and `Back Extra` is optional. `Back Extra` is shown on the answer side, so use it for an explanation or a source.

`Text` must contain at least one valid cloze marker. The shortest form is `<<clz answer>>`:

```
The capital of China is <<clz Beijing>>.
```

This exports to Anki as:

```
The capital of China is {{c1::Beijing}}.
```

`<<clz>>` always uses `c1`. To control the number, use `<<c1>>` through `<<c9>>`:

```
The capital of <<c1 China>> is <<c2 Beijing>>.
```

Each number produces its own card in Anki, while markers that share a number are revealed together on the same card. With the example above, Anki gets two cards: one asking for the country, one asking for the capital.

Quote answers that contain spaces:

```
<<clz "New York">>
<<c2 "New York">>
```

In the card preview, cloze answers are blurred until you hover over the card.

!! 4. LaTeX

Install the [[LaTeX plugin|https://tiddlywiki.com/plugins/tiddlywiki/latex/]] first; the preview renders formulas with it, and Anki renders the exported formulas with MathJax.

Use `<<ltx>>` in any field. By default it inserts a block formula:

```
<<ltx "\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{f^{(n)}(a)}{n!}(x-a)^n">>
```

Add `inline` as the second argument for a formula inside a sentence:

```
The mass-energy equivalence is <<ltx "E = mc^2" inline>>.
```

